1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:08,779
A school bag!

3
00:00:09,079 --> 00:00:11,749
Its strap must bend, and it must not tear.

4
00:00:12,029 --> 00:00:13,839
Which material would you choose?

5
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:14,974
One, fabric.

6
00:00:16,564 --> 00:00:17,534
Two, metal.

7
00:00:19,114 --> 00:00:20,114
Three, wood.

8
00:00:21,962 --> 00:00:23,472
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:25,944 --> 00:00:27,404
You against the Buddies!

10
00:00:27,674 --> 00:00:28,904
Lock in first.

11
00:00:29,174 --> 00:00:30,984
One finger for every point.

12
00:00:31,274 --> 00:00:34,014
A little butterfly is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:34,264 --> 00:00:35,504
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:37,225
Today you'll learn:

15
00:00:37,422 --> 00:00:38,762
What engineers do.

16
00:00:38,963 --> 00:00:40,243
The design steps.

17
00:00:40,443 --> 00:00:41,813
Design a school bag.

18
00:00:42,318 --> 00:00:43,258
Are you ready?

19
00:00:43,698 --> 00:00:44,468
Three!

20
00:00:44,848 --> 00:00:45,508
Two!

21
00:00:45,878 --> 00:00:46,528
One!

22
00:00:46,948 --> 00:00:47,668
Go!

23
00:00:49,057 --> 00:00:51,587
Round one: the question from last time!

24
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:53,477
Fabric, metal, or wood?

25
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,077
Show me your fingers!

26
00:00:58,549 --> 00:00:59,529
Locked in!

27
00:00:59,657 --> 00:01:00,267
Two!

28
00:01:00,447 --> 00:01:01,187
Metal!

29
00:01:01,357 --> 00:01:02,757
Nothing can tear that!

30
00:01:02,807 --> 00:01:03,487
Three!

31
00:01:03,787 --> 00:01:04,947
Wood is strong!

32
00:01:05,002 --> 00:01:05,592
One.

33
00:01:06,012 --> 00:01:08,192
My strap bends over my shoulder.

34
00:01:09,141 --> 00:01:10,291
Look closer.

35
00:01:10,861 --> 00:01:13,221
Three straps, over the back of a chair.

36
00:01:13,345 --> 00:01:15,465
The fabric strap bends round it.

37
00:01:16,035 --> 00:01:17,605
Fabric is flexible.

38
00:01:17,711 --> 00:01:19,511
The metal bar stays straight.

39
00:01:20,071 --> 00:01:21,861
The wooden stick stays straight.

40
00:01:22,431 --> 00:01:23,941
No good on a shoulder!

41
00:01:27,353 --> 00:01:30,383
Now the fabric strap lifts a bag full of books.

42
00:01:30,963 --> 00:01:31,913
No tear!

43
00:01:32,503 --> 00:01:33,863
Fabric is strong.

44
00:01:37,002 --> 00:01:38,302
The answer is one.

45
00:01:38,602 --> 00:01:39,452
Fabric!

46
00:01:39,732 --> 00:01:40,712
One finger?

47
00:01:41,032 --> 00:01:42,232
One finger up!

48
00:01:42,430 --> 00:01:43,160
Oops.

49
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,860
A metal bar on my shoulder?

50
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:45,900
Ouch!

51
00:01:46,029 --> 00:01:47,249
We did not guess.

52
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:48,999
We checked the properties.

53
00:01:49,269 --> 00:01:51,159
That is what engineers do!

54
00:01:52,109 --> 00:01:53,799
So we are engineers too!

55
00:01:53,846 --> 00:01:56,476
Engineers design and make new products.

56
00:01:56,838 --> 00:01:57,988
Say it with me!

57
00:01:58,702 --> 00:02:03,022
Knowing the physical properties of a material is important when designing and

58
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:04,632
making new products.

59
00:02:08,084 --> 00:02:09,874
Engineers follow a plan.

60
00:02:10,154 --> 00:02:12,174
First: what is the object for?

61
00:02:12,826 --> 00:02:13,956
Look closer.

62
00:02:14,566 --> 00:02:15,656
Books go in.

63
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:18,906
A school bag is for carrying books to school.

64
00:02:21,226 --> 00:02:22,706
Then: its parts.

65
00:02:23,356 --> 00:02:24,216
Straps.

66
00:02:24,786 --> 00:02:25,716
A body.

67
00:02:26,306 --> 00:02:27,196
A zip.

68
00:02:27,766 --> 00:02:28,726
A base.

69
00:02:28,842 --> 00:02:32,462
And what each part must do: its intended use.

70
00:02:33,172 --> 00:02:34,812
The straps carry the bag.

71
00:02:35,412 --> 00:02:37,092
The body holds the books.

72
00:02:37,672 --> 00:02:39,532
The zip opens and closes.

73
00:02:40,102 --> 00:02:41,872
The base sits on the floor.

74
00:02:45,097 --> 00:02:47,117
Fabric is flexible and strong.

75
00:02:47,297 --> 00:02:49,587
So I will make every part of fabric!

76
00:02:49,708 --> 00:02:51,268
Something is not right.

77
00:02:51,538 --> 00:02:53,718
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

78
00:02:53,998 --> 00:02:54,958
Hold on!

79
00:03:00,371 --> 00:03:01,501
Arms crossed?

80
00:03:01,771 --> 00:03:02,931
One finger up!

81
00:03:03,221 --> 00:03:05,011
Each part has its own use.

82
00:03:05,281 --> 00:03:07,121
So we choose part by part.

83
00:03:07,474 --> 00:03:08,414
Hold on, Pip!

84
00:03:08,594 --> 00:03:10,854
My bag sits on a wet canteen floor!

85
00:03:11,278 --> 00:03:12,858
Now we draw the design.

86
00:03:13,148 --> 00:03:14,258
Look closer.

87
00:03:18,568 --> 00:03:19,908
Last, we choose.

88
00:03:20,478 --> 00:03:21,838
Part by part.

89
00:03:21,895 --> 00:03:23,465
The base: plastic.

90
00:03:24,045 --> 00:03:26,185
The drop of water stays on top.

91
00:03:26,725 --> 00:03:28,575
Plastic is waterproof.

92
00:03:28,638 --> 00:03:30,138
The zip: metal.

93
00:03:30,748 --> 00:03:32,828
Open, close, open, close.

94
00:03:33,428 --> 00:03:34,448
No break.

95
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,318
Metal is strong.

96
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:38,762
The straps and the body: fabric.

97
00:03:39,332 --> 00:03:40,872
Flexible and strong.

98
00:03:44,019 --> 00:03:44,739
Oh!

99
00:03:44,989 --> 00:03:47,409
A fabric base would soak up the water!

100
00:03:47,839 --> 00:03:49,089
Say it with me!

101
00:03:49,801 --> 00:03:53,411
The materials are selected for the different functions of the parts based

102
00:03:53,431 --> 00:03:55,061
on their physical properties.

103
00:03:57,691 --> 00:03:58,581
Be a book!

104
00:03:58,861 --> 00:03:59,851
Shrink down.

105
00:04:00,131 --> 00:04:01,061
Quietly.

106
00:04:03,343 --> 00:04:05,763
You are a book, inside the school bag.

107
00:04:06,426 --> 00:04:07,166
Zip!

108
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:09,916
The metal zip closes above you.

109
00:04:10,579 --> 00:04:12,539
The fabric straps pull tight.

110
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:14,359
Up you go!

111
00:04:15,017 --> 00:04:15,737
Bump!

112
00:04:16,577 --> 00:04:17,667
A wet floor.

113
00:04:18,457 --> 00:04:20,727
The plastic base keeps the water out.

114
00:04:21,497 --> 00:04:22,757
You stay dry!

115
00:04:24,332 --> 00:04:25,792
Show me your score hand!

116
00:04:26,072 --> 00:04:27,462
One finger or more?

117
00:04:27,782 --> 00:04:29,142
You beat the Buddies.

118
00:04:29,412 --> 00:04:30,442
Two fingers?

119
00:04:30,722 --> 00:04:31,732
High five!

120
00:04:32,304 --> 00:04:33,964
Did you spot the butterfly?

121
00:04:34,244 --> 00:04:36,134
It was on the plant by the window!

122
00:04:36,404 --> 00:04:37,704
Tell someone at home.

123
00:04:38,432 --> 00:04:40,632
Let's read today's key words together!

124
00:04:40,922 --> 00:04:41,682
Ready?

125
00:04:41,969 --> 00:04:42,939
Engineers.

126
00:04:44,504 --> 00:04:45,364
Design.

127
00:04:46,734 --> 00:04:48,024
Intended use.

128
00:04:49,727 --> 00:04:50,667
Well done!

129
00:04:51,464 --> 00:04:52,674
Our design is done!

130
00:04:52,824 --> 00:04:54,427
Let's make a thousand bags!

131
00:04:54,447 --> 00:04:55,707
Not yet, Basil!

132
00:04:56,007 --> 00:04:57,767
Will the new strap really hold?

133
00:04:58,057 --> 00:04:59,687
Engineers do not guess.

134
00:04:59,957 --> 00:05:00,957
They test!

135
00:05:01,016 --> 00:05:02,606
Find out in Part Two!

136
00:05:03,766 --> 00:05:04,867
Say it with us!

137
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:06,417
Ready?

138
00:05:06,541 --> 00:05:07,201
One!

139
00:05:07,541 --> 00:05:08,241
two!

140
00:05:08,546 --> 00:05:09,721
Now you know!
